<title>USA: Mitel stake cut by Quebec agency.</title>
<headline>Mitel stake cut by Quebec agency.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caisse de depot du Quebec said Tuesday it cut its stake in Mitel Corp to 4.67 percent or 5,010,647 common shares.</p>
<p>In a filing with Securities and Exchange Commission, the investment agency said its latest transactions include a net 659,000 common shares sold between Dec 19 and Jan 14 at C$8.73 to C$9.02 per share.</p>
<p>The agency holds the stake for investment.</p>
<p>Mitel, of Kanata, Ont., Canada, makes electronic telecommunications products and semiconductor devices.</p>
</text>
